# Copy to server/.env
#
# If the API connects to the wrong Postgres port: check Windows "Environment Variables"
# for a user/system DATABASE_URL (e.g. an old Prisma dev port). Remove it or update it;
# the app loads server/.env with override in development, but tools that skip env.ts may not.
#
# 1) Start Prisma dev and KEEP IT RUNNING:
#      cd server && npx prisma dev
# 2) Copy the DATABASE_URL line from that terminal output (not SHADOW_DATABASE_URL).
#    Current Prisma dev often uses localhost:51214 and database `template1`.
#    If migrate says "Can't reach ...", your .env port/DB name does not match what `prisma dev` printed.
#
# 3) "Skipped! already running" = OK; another prisma dev is up — do not start a second default.
#
# 4) Migrations (no shadow DB on Prisma dev):  npm run prisma:migrate:deploy
#
# 5) Node may log "ExperimentalWarning: SQLite" from Prisma dev internals — safe to ignore.
#
DATABASE_URL="postgresql://postgres:postgres@127.0.0.1:51214/template1?sslmode=disable&pgbouncer=true"
JWT_SECRET="paste-your-generated-jwt-secret-here"
NODE_ENV=development

# Optional Docker Postgres (repo root: docker compose up -d):
# DATABASE_URL="postgresql://postgres:cstp_local_dev@127.0.0.1:5433/cstp"
